### Sample requests for spring-mcp-client.
### In IntelliJ, open this file and click the green ▶ next to a request.
### Start spring-mcp-server (port 8080) and this client (port 8081) first.

### ---------- Chat with Claude (uses the server's tools) ----------

### Weather question (public tools, no server API key needed)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Do I need an umbrella in Dhaka tomorrow?"
}

### Follow-up in the same conversation (paste the conversationId from the previous reply)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "PASTE-ID-HERE",
  "message": "And the day after?"
}

### Task question (needs MCP_SERVER_API_KEY)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Add a high priority task to renew my passport by next Friday, then show my open tasks."
}

### ---------- Run the server's prompts ----------

### Plan my day
POST http://localhost:8081/api/prompts/plan_my_day
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "arguments": { "city": "Dhaka" }
}

### Trip prep
POST http://localhost:8081/api/prompts/trip_prep
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "arguments": { "city": "London", "days": "5" }
}

### Weekly review (no arguments)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/prompts/weekly_review

### ---------- Explore the MCP server (no AI) ----------

### Server info and instructions
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/server

### Tools
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/tools

### Resources and templates
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/resources

### Read a resource
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/resources/read?uri=weather://Dhaka

### Read your open tasks (needs MCP_SERVER_API_KEY)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/resources/read?uri=tasks://open

### Prompts
GET http://localhost:8081/api/mcp/prompts
